# An L-shaped room, 3 m high, for examples/room_3d.py and tests/test_room3d.py.
# Footprint (meters): an 8 x 3 hall along x, with a 4 x 3 wing along y at its left end.
# Walls are quads, split where they meet so that neighbouring faces share their edges.
# floor (z = 0): p0..p7
v 0 0 0
v 4 0 0
v 8 0 0
v 8 3 0
v 4 3 0
v 0 3 0
v 4 6 0
v 0 6 0
# ceiling (z = 3): p0..p7
v 0 0 3
v 4 0 3
v 8 0 3
v 8 3 3
v 4 3 3
v 0 3 3
v 4 6 3
v 0 6 3
# floor
f 1 2 5 6
f 2 3 4 5
f 6 5 7 8
# ceiling
f 9 14 13 10
f 10 13 12 11
f 14 16 15 13
# walls, around the footprint
f 1 9 10 2
f 2 10 11 3
f 3 11 12 4
f 4 12 13 5
f 5 13 15 7
f 7 15 16 8
f 8 16 14 6
f 6 14 9 1
